institution: "Sylhet International University"
department: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering"
repository-code: "https://github.com/imrankhansaami/RADAR_Hybrid_Feature_Selection_Thesis"
abstract: >-
  Bachelor's thesis that re-implements and compares two feature-selection
  strategies for ransomware detection on the RADAR Sysmon event dataset --
  consensus voting (FS-A) and the percentage sweep with a combined score
  (FS-B) -- and proposes a voting-ranked sweep (FS-C) that links the two.
  The subsets are evaluated with seven classical classifiers and the A2G-PTH
  deep model under a paper-faithful random split, a leakage-aware group split,
  and a chronological drift split, with repeated seeds and computational-cost
  measurements.
keywords:
  - feature selection
  - ransomware detection
  - Sysmon
  - RADAR dataset
  - machine learning
  - concept drift
